    "frames_per_trial": [
      256,
      256,
      32
    ],
    "timing": "One untimed warmup and one byte-verification trial per version/size, followed by eight alternating A/B and B/A trials. Packet creation outside timing. Whole final payload, frame count and ACK count checked in verification trials.",
    "baseline": "HEAD AVC420VideoPlayer before this release, identified by revision and module SHA-256.",
    "candidate": "Working-tree AVC420VideoPlayer, identified by module SHA-256. Equivalent change applied to AVC444VideoPlayer.",
    "legacy": "Candidate with Uint8Array.fromBase64 unavailable, byte/frame/ACK verification only; not included in timing summaries."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "CPU timings cover parser/assembly/inspection only. They do not measure native H.264 decode, GPU work, network, Wi-Fi jitter, live session latency, frame rate or the old client laptop.",
    "A modern Chrome with Uint8Array.fromBase64 was measured. Older browsers continue using the existing binary-string/manual-copy path and do not gain this native-decoding speedup.",
    "Synthetic payloads exercise byte parsing and scanning; the encoded bytes are not decoded by a real codec during this benchmark. Separate real WebCodecs integration tests validate actual H.264 streams.",
    "Native Base64 produces a bounded temporary byte array before copying into the existing bounded envelope; this does not claim zero-copy assembly or lower peak payload memory.",
    "Means summarize fixed-count trials; no frame percentiles, GC pause, GPU counter or heap-pressure measurement is inferred."
  ],
